<%# THE LAB'S OWN FEW RULES, on top of the `debug` layout's and in its palette --
    NO NEW COLOURS. Every value below is already in
    `app/views/layouts/debug.html.erb`; `app/views/map/_styles.html.erb` is the
    precedent for a page adding its own without touching the layout.

    THE ONE IDEA IS THE PURPLE/TEAL CONVENTION, which is the README's turn
    diagram's and the debug view's `.branch` colours: PURPLE is a model call,
    TEAL is the app deciding from records it holds. The sample page is one column
    in sequence and every step in it is marked one or the other, because the
    thing the captain said he cannot hold in his head is exactly which of the two
    each step was. %>
<style>
  /* One step of the sequence. The rule down the left is what makes the column
     read as an order rather than as a stack of panels. */
  .step { border-left: 2px solid #21262c; padding: 0 0 0 .8rem; margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }
  .step.model { border-left-color: #4a3d5c; }
  .step.engine { border-left-color: #2f5a50; }
  .step > h3 { margin-top: 0; }

  /* Who decided it. Same two colours the debug view's `.branch` gives an
     arrival and a conversation, for the same reason. */
  .who { padding: 0 .35rem; border: 1px solid; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 11px; }
  .who.model { color: #b79ad8; border-color: #4a3d5c; }
  .who.engine { color: #7fd8c0; border-color: #2f5a50; }

  /* A pick against an expectation. Teal and the warn colour, so a miss reads the
     same way a flag does. */
  .pick.hit { color: #7fd8c0; }
  .pick.miss { color: #d88f7f; }
  .pick.unscored { color: #6b737b; }

  /* The checkbox groups on the kind form, inline so seven picks fit on a screen. */
  .lab-choice { display: inline-block; margin: 0 .9rem .2rem 0; color: #cfd3d8; white-space: nowrap; }
  .lab-form input[type="text"], .lab-form textarea, .lab-form select {
    background: #08090b; color: #cfd3d8; border: 1px solid #21262c;
    font: inherit; padding: .2rem .3rem;
  }
  .lab-form input[type="submit"] {
    background: #14140f; color: #d8c07f; border: 1px solid #4a4326;
    font: inherit; padding: .3rem .8rem; cursor: pointer;
  }
  /* The one button in the app that spends money gets the warn border, so it
     cannot be clicked by mistake for a link. */
  form.button_to input[type="submit"] {
    background: #12151a; color: #cfd3d8; border: 1px solid #33393f;
    font: inherit; padding: .3rem .8rem; cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>
